From: Scott C DeLancey <delancey@darkwing.uoregon.edu>
Subject: CULTURE/EVOL: Was Bavarian Pig/Generalizing from primates 

On Fri, 9 Jul 1993, Perry E. Metzger wrote:

> Are they Bonobos APES or Bonobos MONKEYS?

They are apes, not monkeys.  That's Jay's mistake.

> In any case, if these are actually pygmy chimps, the Jane Goodall
> stuff I've read would not tend to support the notion that they fuck
> everything in site.

Jane Goodall's stuff has nothing to do with it; she was studying
chimps, not bonobos.  Their social behavior, in particular, is
quite different. Primatologists have adopted the term "bonobo"
to replace the older term "pygmy chimpanzee" in recognition of the
fact that they are a very different species.  This is the point of
Jared Diamond's title, "The Third Chimpanzee", i.e. that chimps,
bonobos, and homo sap comprise a single primate lineage.  My
memory may be exaggerating what I've actually read, but the story
it tells me is that bonobos are not any closer genetically to chimps
than to humans.

Scott DeLancey



